# Offizier (M6, D-096): a k.u.k. officer of the Bad Ischl Kaisertage, the
# tradition regiments' historic parade dress. Dark-blue tunic b/B with an S
# lit edge, Y buttons and a Y/o Feldbinde (sash), a small R collar facing,
# pike-grey trousers i/m with an R stripe, d boots, white gloves w/i, a d/m
# shako with a Y rosette, Y/o band and a green g/G/j plume (all at or below
# row 10 = the hitbox top), a friendly brown handlebar moustache O.
# march: high step (near knee up / far knee up), arms swinging.
# habtacht (telegraph): heels together, arm straight, the sabre half drawn
# (a w/i stub rising from the Y guard at the hip), the scabbard hanging
# straight down behind the back leg.
# praesentiert: the sabre raised vertically in front of the face, blade w/i
# with a k outline in columns 8-11, tip closed by a single k at row 0 (inside the 8x16 sabre zone
# above the hitbox, columns 4-11). Nothing else is drawn above row 10.
# squished: sits on the ground, shako askew, salutes anyway.
# Faces right; mirror = auto. Built with a scratch script (layers + automatic
# k outline, plus a pixel post-pass), frozen to text here.
sprite = offizier
size   = 16x32
origin = 8,32
hitbox = 2,10,12,22
mirror = auto
anim   = march        frames=2 ticks=8 loop
anim   = habtacht     frames=1
anim   = praesentiert frames=1
anim   = squished     frames=1
